xwayland: fullscreen a game at the resolution it set through RandR

An X11 game that changes the resolution through RandR (an exclusive
fullscreen mode, as SDL's SDL_SetWindowFullscreenMode and Wine set one) gets
no new mode under XWayland. XWayland tells that client alone that the monitor
has the mode, and when the client's window is at the monitor's origin and of
that size, it scales the window up to the whole monitor with wp_viewport,
input included. It names the modes it emulates in the client's windows'
_XWAYLAND_RANDR_EMU_MONITOR_RECTS property (x, y, width, height per monitor,
in X11 coordinates), so that the window manager fullscreens them at that
size, as Mutter and KWin do.

Hyprland's XWM did not read the property, and fullscreened such a window at
the monitor's own size: the game drew every pixel of the monitor whatever
resolution it was set to, and XWayland never scaled it. Minecraft set to
1280x720 on a 3840x2400 panel at xwayland:scale 2 drew 4800x3000, 15.6 times
the pixels it asked for.

The XWM now reads the property, at map and as it changes, and a window that
Hyprland gives the whole of a monitor, as fullscreen does, is configured at
the size its client set for that monitor. A change of the mode while
fullscreen is followed at once. A window whose client set no mode, or one
that does not cover the monitor, is configured as before.

For Nova: packaging/hyprland/PKGBUILD applies this to Hyprland 0.57.2's
release tarball after xwayland-scale.patch and release-bind.patch (patch
-Np1); it asks xwaylandSize(), which xwayland-scale.patch adds, for the
monitor's size in X11 coordinates. packaging/hyprland/UPSTREAM.md is the pull
request it is offered as.

